                    "name": "text",
                    "content": {
                      "text": [
                        {
                          "locale": "en",
                          "text": "This as an example of how to use the button enablement maps to disable/enable and hide/show event, navigation and row action buttons. \n<br/>\nThe creation of the map is done as custom code and can be checked out in the devapp example-code (<i>devapp\\src\\customizations\\custom-button-enablement.tsx</i>)\n<br/>\nThe example shows the following\n<ul>\n<li>An event-button in the footer called \"Submit\", which is only enabled when the form is dirty.\n</li>\n<li>\nA custom delete button which is only shown in the first row and hidden in all others. Additonally, the default delete button is hidden in the first row.\n</li>\n<li>\nA copy button which is not enabled in the model but shown anyway as configured in the enablement map\n</li>\n<li>\nA commit button in the detached-repeat detail screen, which is only enabled if the checkbox \"Data Complete\" is checked\n</li>\n<li>\nAn initially disabled navigation button to the second screen as menu entry \"children\" in the sub header, which is only enabled if the checkbox \"children\" is checked\n</li>\n</ul>\n<br/>\nPlease refer to the form-engine documentation for more information about how to construct these enablement maps."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
